dialect protocol
protocol json.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.json
start body

# P2-P1: `stdio.json` is TEXT-NATIVE (per the P2 plan's own classification) — there is no "binary
# JSON"; the pack container IS the SEMIO envelope wrapping the artifact's own RFC8259 text bytes
# verbatim (`ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with` in 🔣️json/…/📸️snapshot/🦀️component.rs:481-507:
# `write_json_text(&self.value).into_bytes()` passed straight to `store::semio_format::wrap_binary`
# — no `pack_rt::encode_document` structured record, because a `JsonValue` document has no
# `RecordSpec` to walk against, same reason `#[derive(dsl::DslArtifact)]` is unusable here).
#
# The framework-level SEMIO envelope itself (magic `0x8953454D0D0A1A0A` + LE u32 token length +
# UTF-8 token) is described ONCE, at
# `🧰️framework/🛍️products/💻️os/🔨️modules/🧬️semio/📡️protocol/📡️component.protocol.semio`
# (P2-M3 deliverable 3) — this file does NOT re-describe that framing. Per that file's own report
# (`p2-m3-report.md` §5 point 4) and confirmed directly against the REAL harness this file is
# validated by (`m5_handcrafted_protocol_conformance`'s `inner_payload_from_semio_example` in
# `🧪️fixture-sweep/🦀️component.rs`, which calls `unwrap_binary` and hands `walk_protocol` only the
# INNER bytes): this file models the bytes as if the walk already starts AT the payload, past the
# envelope. Cross-artifact `use semio.envelope` is not yet functional (P2-M3 confirmed), so the
# envelope is deliberately NOT re-inlined here either — the payload-only framing below is both the
# honest current mechanism boundary and the literal shape the real test exercises.
#
# The payload itself is opaque, unstructured UTF-8 bytes at the BINARY layer by construction (its
# real internal grammar — object/array/string/number recursion — is `📝️text/📖️component.grammar.semio`'s
# job, not the protocol dialect's; RFC8259 nesting has no fixed byte width to declare here) — `chain
# ... utf8` is the honest boundary, the same treatment `binary/raw`'s protocol precedent gives an
# opaque payload segment.
framing record
chain payload utf8
